=== PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end) ===
  Data sources (web hooks → P1/S8 seams; no HTTP in the view):
    - useAuthStatus            -> TeslaAuthStatusProviding (.loaded(authenticated,expiresAt)
                                  / .empty / .failed / .offline) + the two document signals
                                  teslasync:tesla-auth-expired/-recovered (.tokenExpiredSignal /
                                  .tokenRecoveredSignal → pillDisconnected).
    - useAuthURL               -> TeslaAccountActing.connect() → outcome .authURL(url) →
                                  onOpenAuthURL (web window.location.href = data.auth_url).
    - useRefreshAuth           -> .refreshToken() → .refreshed (+ status refetch).
    - useSyncVehicles          -> .syncVehicles() → .synced(count) (inline "Synced N").
    - useDisconnectAuth        -> .disconnect() → .disconnected (+ status refetch).
    - useToast                 -> inline feedback banner (success/danger + detail).
    - useConfirm/ConfirmDialog -> native .alert (destructive confirm + cancel).
    - notifyTeslaAuthRecovered -> onAuthRecovered fired on the unauth→auth edge only.
  Composition (web GlassPanel/IconBox/Button/ConfirmDialog/FadeIn → platform tokens):
    GlassPanel→TSGlassPanel, IconBox→TSIconBox(tone:.accent), Button(primary/secondary/
    danger + cyan re-authorize)→TSButton(.primary/.secondary/.destructive/.ghost),
    Badge pill→TSBadge/warning capsule, FadeIn→TSFadeIn. No Tailwind ported; no raw hex.
  Logic parity: expiringSoon (authed & 0<remaining<=7d → max(1,ceil(d))); status box
    connected(green check + expiry pill + "Token expires {datetime}") / disconnected(red
    cross + reconnect body) / not-connected; button set gated on authenticated; sync-
    success inline line. States added for the P4 leaf contract: loading/empty/error +
    the orthogonal live/stale/offline freshness axis (chip+banner+one-shot auto-refresh).
  i18n: 22/22 web source keys present verbatim (tesla.*, toast.*, common.cancel); 11
